00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:33.140
JIMMY TRAN: Identity
Access Management

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.620
is how you decide who can do
what with your Google Cloud

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.790
resources.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.020
You can get incredibly specific
when you create an IAM policy,

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.900
but essentially, you
have an identity, a role,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.549
and a resource.

00:00:45.549 --> 00:00:47.840
HEATHER CROSS: Think of it
as an air traffic controller

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.070
for your business.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.320
An organization's internal
structure and policies

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.240
can get complex fast.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.430
Projects, work
groups, and managing

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.430
who has authorization to do
what can change dynamically.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.990
JIMMY TRAN: Cloud
IAM is designed

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.120
with a clean
universal interface,

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.550
so you're able to manage access
control across all Google Cloud

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:09.567
Platform resources consistently
from App Engine to GCE.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.150
HEATHER CROSS: Keep
in mind, Cloud IAM

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:14.140
is offered at no additional
charge for GCP customers.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.959
You'll only be charged
for use of other services.

00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:20.452
[MUSIC PLAYING]

