00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.680
Speaking of G Suite, Cloud
IAM supports standard Google

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:35.360
accounts.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.390
That means you can
manage users and groups

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.370
through the Google Admin
console, all in one place.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.620
HEATHER CROSS: You can
create cloud IAM policies,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.290
granting permission to a
Google group, a Google hosted

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.160
domain, a service account, or
specific Google account holders

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.602
using Cloud Identity.

00:01:50.602 --> 00:01:53.836
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.030
JIMMY TRAN: A full audit trail
of permissions authorization,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.030
removal, and delegation
is surfaced automatically

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.290
for your admins.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.660
Cloud IAM lets you focus
on business policies

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.530
around your resources and
makes compliance easy.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.280
HEATHER CROSS: For
established enterprises

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.620
with complex
organizational structures,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.500
hundreds of work groups, and
potentially many more projects,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.740
Cloud IAM provides a unified
view and a security policy

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.920
across your entire organization
with built-in auditing

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.057
to ease compliance processes.

00:02:23.057 --> 00:02:26.536
