00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.690
Let's jump into the lab.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.510
We're joining the lab at the
section where user one removes

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.300
project access from user two.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.630
This task easily shows how
to add and remove permissions

00:02:58.630 --> 00:02:59.890
to a user.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.020
Here's what happens.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.870
At this point in the
lab, as user one,

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.870
you have a Google
Cloud Storage bucket.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.070
User two currently has
access to the file.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:17.620
Now, as user one, remove
user two's permissions.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.180
As user two, try to
access the file and fail.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.650
Now, back to user one.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:28.150
Give user two permission
to view the bucket.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.512
Finally, as user two,
access the bucket.

